    "title": "Fact Check: Caitlin Clark wore 'I deserve NBA money' shirt at 2025 WNBA All-Star Game? - NewsBreak",
    "text": "In July 2025, a photo circulated online that purportedly showed WNBA star Caitlin Clark wearing a T-shirt that had the words \"I deserve NBA money\" printed on it. For example, multiple ( archived ) Instagram users shared ( archived ) the picture, amassing thousands of likes on their posts. The image also appeared on Facebook ( archived ) and Threads ( archived ).\nSome people seemed to believe the photo authentically showed Clark wearing a T-shirt demanding she be paid an NBA salary. However, a Google search produced no evidence that she did. Rather, the picture originated from an NBACentel post ( archived ) viewed more than 57 million times as of this writing. NBACentel is an X account that describes its content as parody. Its bio states: \"Featured on @ESPN, @BarstoolSports, @SINoW, @FoxSports, @ComplexSports | PARODY Account. NOT Affiliated with @TheDunkCentral .\" NBACentel posted the image on July 19, the night of the 2025 WNBA All-Star Game . Photos on Getty Images showed that before the game commenced, the participating players, including Clark, actually wore identical T-shirts that had the words \"Pay us what you owe us\" printed on them instead . Snopes has addressed satirical claims shared by NBACentel in the past, including a rumor regarding a fabricated LeBron James quote about music mogul Diddy in September 2024. Snopes has also addressed numerous claims regarding Clark . For background, here is why we alert readers to rumors created by sources that call their output humorous or satirical.",
